- ArtAnno product **wont_wire**; skip Image-gen local wire.

## Verification-gated persist/pivot runtime (Argus / K253)

- Separate Manager/Planner/Engineer from independent Reviewer; admit memories/skills only after review (+ task-native verify when available).
- Persist while evidence supports; pivot on measured failure. Durable project state across sessions.
- `lbx154/Argus` **NO-GO** clone until LICENSE/SPDX present (pyproject MIT claim insufficient). **wont_wire**.

## Hardware-confined agent signing (K254)

- Do not put production signing/SSH/API private keys in agent-readable env, workspace files, or container memory for LIVE/high-blast agents.
- Prefer PKCS#11 / hardware (or OS-isolated) keystores so the host only sees opaque handles + signatures (pairs K239).
- SoftHSM = reproducibility proxy only — not tamper resistance. Anonymous paper artifact **NO-GO** clone until public SPDX.
- Entity `hardware-keystore-mcp-signing` = `policy_wired`.

## Interpretable agentic document ops (READ / K255)

- For long table-heavy / financial-style docs: prefer grep · outline · bounded span reads (or BM25) before dense top-k RAG.
- Require citable line/locator ranges in answers (pairs claim-centered / Traceable Scholarship).
- BM25 can match agentic READ — do not overclaim “agent beats lexical.”
- `.local/adopts/READ` = MIT REFERENCE; **wont_wire** as default CCC MCP.

## Trajectory error-lifecycle attribution (TrajDebug / K256)

- On failed long-horizon sessions: locate earliest wrong commitment with verbatim evidence, not only the terminal symptom.
- Prefer evidence-grounded attribution before LLM-as-judge for “what went wrong” (pairs K242).
- `.local/adopts/TrajDebug` = MIT skeleton (0 `.py` at Phase-0) — **wont_wire** until detector code ships.

## Anytime-valid agent eval stopping (AV-AIVAT / K257)

- Costly agent-vs-agent evals (esp. poker/IIG): prefer variance-reduced + anytime-valid confidence sequences over fixed budgets or naive CI peeking.
- Online value corrections must not use the current game. Release stop metadata for third-party recheck.
- No public AV-AIVAT artifact — pattern only; poker Arena brief. **wont_wire**.

## Programmatic vs JSON tool calling (PTC / K258)

- For code-capable lanes with a sandboxed executor: prefer typed stubs + script composition for multi-tool chains and fan-out (pairs code-as-agent-harness / Code Mode).
- Keep JSON schemas for weak models or when code exec is banned; stubs remain schema-bound / Prebind-gated.
- No public PTC eval harness — **policy_wired** only. Entity `programmatic-tool-calling-ptc`.

## MCP claim validation + NL→tool parameter grounding (CASCADE / K259)

- Before LIVE/high-blast MCP exposure: validate the **claim class** the tool report repeats against ground truth or a stated proxy — membership checks are not enough (pairs K172 / Traceable Scholarship).
- Prefer **server-side** alias/enum normalization over trusting model-filled strings.
- Ambiguous required fields: clarify or refuse — do not silent-default; “if unset” guards miss confident wrong fills (pairs K244).
- Small local models need stricter schema enforcement; larger models reduce schema fails but not confident-wrong defaults.
- `.local/adopts/CASCADE` = MIT REFERENCE (cancer genomics OOD) — **wont_wire** runtime; do not download DepMap/model into the adopt shelf.
- Entity `cascade-mcp` = `wont_wire`; concept `mcp-claim-validation-and-parameter-grounding` = `policy_wired`.

## Adversarial curriculum + doc fidelity (ResidencyRL / K260)

- Long-horizon / multi-turn evals and red-team packs: include **adversarial** and **information-asymmetric** cases, not only cooperative happy-path.
- Score with rubrics **plus** hard fidelity/safety penalties (fabricated durable facts, missed required checks, unsafe shortcuts).
- Gate `done`/terminate on **required-check coverage** — resist premature closure.
- Durable artifacts (notes, Discord, wiki claims, tool reports): **elicited/observed facts only** — never invent fields to fill a schema (pairs Traceable Scholarship / K259).
- Required clarifications under deflection: re-ask once with rationale, then refuse/escalate — do not invent answers (pairs K244).
- Soft autoraters OK as advisory signal; prefer execution verify when available (pairs K162). ResidencyRL code **NO-GO** (Google closed; clinical OOD) — no `.local/adopts/` shelf.
- Entity `residencyrl` = `wont_wire`; concept `adversarial-curriculum-structured-reward-doc-fidelity` = `policy_wired`.


## Reversible context eviction (Blast Radius / K265)

- Prefer **reversible, verification-licensed** eviction over lossy truncation/summarization in long agentic coding loops.
- Estimate prompt reach (context retention + churn-weighted code surface) before sweeping dead mass.
- Archive buried bodies byte-exact (midden) with secret redaction; leave scent skeletons; bound exhumation cost.
- Treat recurring build/test/VCS transcripts as **recurring dead matter** — bury recurrence classes, do not re-pay carry cost every turn.
- Layering: gate/verification decides *whether* a record may replace context; blast-radius scoping decides *which* bodies and *how much* headroom.
- No public Chalk/Blast Radius SPDX clone at Phase-0 — **policy_wired** pattern only; entity `blast-radius-necrophoresis` = `wont_wire`.


## Scaffold over tool interface (K262)

- When measuring MCP vs CLI (or any transport): treat **agent scaffolding** as the primary axis — prompts, control flow, memory, verification — not the interface brand.
- Prefer completion checks via **external state** (repo/tests/prod observe), not agent self-report.
- MCP is not required for every task class; CLI-only scaffolds can be complete (paper 2608.08654).

## Versioned model–harness continual adaptation (Macaron / K263)

- Prefer **versioned model+harness pairs** with parent/data/eval provenance when iterating agent stacks.
- Successor construction under an **external** eval contract — no closed loop that rewrites its own pass criteria (pairs K162).
- Mixture-of-LoRA / specialist adapters = vocabulary only — **no** Macaron/Venti weight downloads; `hcp-sdk` null SPDX **NO-GO** clone.

